 ## Overview
-This method computes the direct illumination contribution for a surface or volume element by combining Lambertian diffuse reflection, an ambient floor, emissive terms, and a non-standard GGX-like specular highlight. It is distinguished from standard PBR implementations by its specific half-vector definition ($H = \text{normalize}(L - V)$) and its integration into voxel-based or splat-based rendering pipelines where immediate shading precedes rasterization or splatting. It serves as the local illumination component in broader light transport simulations, building on [Lighting Models](2056-lighting-models.md).
+This method computes direct illumination for a surface or volume element by combining Lambertian diffuse reflection, an ambient floor, emissive contributions, and a non-standard GGX-like specular highlight [S1, unofficial]. It is distinguished from standard microfacet implementations by its half-vector definition ($H = \text{normalize}(L - V)$) and its use in voxel or splat-based pipelines where shading is applied immediately before rasterization or splatting [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It serves as the local illumination component in broader light transport simulations, building on [Lighting Models](2056-lighting-models.md).
 
